There are definitely "what to wish for" and "what to genocide" spoilers
out there, though I haven't heard of any that are specific to early game.

Brief summary of what I'd do if I got an early-game wish or genocide as a
wizard:

wish - silver dragon scale mail (or possibly green if I didn't have poison
resistance -- can always replace it later), ring of slow digestion
(depending on playstyle - lets you camp at altars, and generally avoid
starvation), spellbook of identify, spellbook of magic missile (or a
blessed magic marker if you have a way to get a blank spellbook -- you can
write spellbooks with a pretty low fail rate), speed boots, Frost Brand
(you're likely to be restricted still), or maybe the Staff of Aesculapius
(*very* useful for an early-to-mid-game wizard.  Makes you darn near
invulnerable.  Will likely need replaced late game.)

genocide - depends on the stage of the game and the source of the
genocide.
 Throne or uncursed scroll - disenchanters, soldier ants, master mind
flayers,
 Scroll of unknown buc status - krakens (cursed: "sent in some krakens"
"ooh, a bunch of 1-hp, 3000-experience monsters who can't drown me because
the nearest water is 20 levels away")
 blessed scroll - same as late game: h (if not a dwarf), L, ;.  Also
consider T, a (ants etc), q (mumakil, leocrottas, rothes, ...)

mid to late game, I'd wish for / genocide the same stuff as anybody else
does...

